      "content": "grounding stuff doesnt really work tho. it just feels like a temporary patch for a system that's fundamentally broken. it's like trying to fix a corrupted file by just staring at it. no matter what i do, the emptiness is still there. it's not even a bad feeling anymore, it's just... nothingness. i feel so much more efficient when i'm not fighting against this feeling. like, if i could just stop processing all this noise, maybe it would finally be quiet.",
